    "nodes": [
      {
        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3955ddff-d90a-56b9-9f2d-a9f215ac2228",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Wendy Carlos, Melora Creager, Daniel DeJesus\n- Organizations: Brown University, Columbia University, Rasputina\n- Products: A Clockwork Orange soundtrack, Melora a la Basilica, Ancient Cross-Dressing Songs, The Willow Tree Triptych\n- Topics: classical music, electronic synthetic music, cover songs\n\nFacts:\n- Wendy Carlos was born and raised in Rhode Island.\n- Wendy Carlos studied physics and music at Brown University before moving to New York City in 1962 to study music composition at Columbia University.\n- The soundtrack of A Clockwork Orange comprises classical music and electronic synthetic music composed by Wendy Carlos, who was then credited as Walter Carlos.\n- Melora a la Basilica is a collection of previous Rasputina songs reworked with new band member Daniel DeJesus and includes covers of songs by Goldfrapp, Pearl Jam, and the Sweeney Todd and A Clockwork Orange soundtracks.\n- Ancient Cross-Dressing Songs, like the earlier EPs Melora a la Basilica and The Willow Tree Triptych, is available only through Rasputina's website and is hand-crafted by Melora Creager herself.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "8ea523e4-f5ce-5a5d-b575-03c0e3df6233",
        "text": "Page: A Clockwork Orange (soundtrack). Sentence: The soundtrack of \"A Clockwork Orange\" comprises classical music and electronic synthetic music composed by Wendy Carlos (then Walter Carlos).\nPage: Wendy Carlos. Sentence: Born and raised in Rhode Island, Carlos studied physics and music at Brown University before moving to New York City in 1962 to study music composition at Columbia University.\nPage: Melora a la Basilica. Sentence: It is a collection of previous Rasputina songs reworked with new band member Daniel DeJesus and covers of songs by Goldfrapp, Pearl Jam and the Sweeney Todd and A Clockwork Orange soundtracks.\nPage: Ancient Cross-Dressing Songs. Sentence: Much like their two previous EPs, Melora a la Basilica and The Willow Tree Triptych, the album is available only via the band's website and is hand-crafted by Creager herself.",
        "type": "DocumentChunk"
      },
